    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver — this is decided on the platform's own records.\n\nOutcome: the 5.00 SGD cancellation fee is refunded in full (FULL_REFUND). The rider gets back the 5.00 SGD shown as 'cancellation_fee' and 'total_charged' on the payments ledger (EV-FARE-05055). No compensation is payable to the driver.\n\nWhy. POL-NS-24 gives the rider a no-charge cancellation where the driver does not arrive at the pickup by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes. The scheduled pickup was 07:30 (EV-TRIP-05055), so the deadline was 07:35. The trip record carries no arrival event at all — arrived_at is null and arrived_by_deadline is false. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05055, complete, 50 fixes at 30-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gap over 120 seconds) independently confirms it: no fix comes within the 50 m arrival radius POL-NS-21 sets for this STANDARD pickup, and the last fixes, from 07:33:10 through the 07:37:40 cancellation, are stationary roughly 1.1 km short of the pickup. The driver therefore did not arrive by 07:35, and the rider's cancellation at 07:37:40 was the cancellation POL-NS-24 permits. The rider's submission that the 5.00 SGD should be returned is accepted.\n\nThe driver's points. I accept that the driver met the contact obligation in POL-NS-23: he sent in-app messages at 07:31:10 and 07:36:30 and placed an answered 40-second in-app call at 07:33:20, all before the cancellation (EV-CHAT-05055, EV-TRIP-05055). That means the fee is not voided on contact grounds, and it also means no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due under POL-NS-24, because that credit needs a failure to attempt contact as well — both sides are right on that point, and no referral arises. But the contact obligation is a separate test; it does not satisfy POL-NS-24's arrival deadline and does not re-authorise the charge. Nor does POL-NS-22 save the fee: it authorises the 5.00 SGD only when the driver cancels after the free wait, whereas here the rider cancelled and no free wait ever began, because under POL-NS-21 the wait for a driver who has not arrived does not run. The ledger figure of 5.00 SGD 'fee_charged_sgd' matching the 5.00 SGD 'policy_fee_sgd' shows only the amount was right, not that the charge was authorised.\n\nThe escalation request under POL-GEN-26 is refused. The facts POL-NS-24 needs — the deadline, whether the driver arrived, and when the rider cancelled — are carried by artifacts the pre-pass graded COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the record affirmatively shows non-arrival rather than leaving it unestablished. The traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05055-01) is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; a missing artifact carries no fact (POL-GEN-02(3)), it is not needed for the no-show test, and it opens no question. The driver's 'jam' account, in his statement and chat messages, explains the delay but POL-NS-24 attaches no traffic defence to the arrival deadline.\n\nAt a contested value of 5.00 SGD, with no fraud flag on either profile and no safety indicator, the AI ruling is final (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26). Because every artifact carrying the deciding fact is at weight 1.0, confidence is not depressed by impairment (POL-GEN-02(2)); I set it at 0.9."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
